---
name: doc-edit
description: >-
  When the user wants a Word file or Google Doc edited: find and replace that
  keeps formatting, fill a template, change a table, suggest changes as tracked
  changes, add comments, or accept or reject changes. Always saves a new copy.
---
# Edit Word files and Google Docs

## Follow the ground rules

- Always save a new copy, such as `Offer - Sample Co - 2026-10-27 - edited.docx`. Never overwrite or delete the original.
- Never write ID numbers in chat.
- Tell the user what you changed and how many times. A count of 0 means no match, so say so.
- When the user wants to review changes before they count, make them tracked changes (Word) or suggestions (Google Docs), not direct edits.

## Pick the route

| The file is | Do this |
|---|---|
| A Google Doc | Edit it with the Google Docs connector (next section). Copy it first with the Google Drive connector when the change is big or the user wants the original kept. |
| A .docx stored in Drive or another cloud | Download it, edit a copy here, and upload the result as a new file next to the original. |
| A .docx on this computer or sent in chat | Edit a copy here. |
| An old .doc | Convert a copy first: `soffice --headless --convert-to docx in.doc`. |

Check the connector's live tool list before the first call, since tool names and fields can change.

## Edit a Google Doc

1. Read the Doc with the read tool. It lists paragraphs and tables with their positions and returns a revision id.
2. Replace text with the replace tool. It changes every match and returns a count. Set `suggest` to make each change a suggestion the owner can accept or reject.
3. For styles, find the text first to get fresh positions, then apply the text or paragraph style. Positions go stale after every write, so find again before each edit and pass the revision id so a clash fails instead of editing the wrong spot.
4. Group several edits into one batch call, because Docs limits writes per minute.
5. Accept or reject suggestions with the matching tools. Read comments and reply with the Google Drive connector.
6. A Doc exported as .docx keeps its suggestions as tracked changes, so the helper below can list, accept, or reject them.
7. Send the link and list the changes.

## Install the Word helper on first use

Run this before any helper command. It writes the helper when it is missing or older than v2.

```bash
mkdir -p ~/.file-agent && f=~/.file-agent/docx_edit.py && grep -qx '# docx_edit.py v2' "$f" 2>/dev/null || cat > "$f" <<'PYEOF'
#!/usr/bin/env python3
# docx_edit.py v2
"""Edit a DOCX and keep its styles. Every edit writes a NEW file and stops if it exists."""
import argparse, copy, json, os, sys
from datetime import datetime, timezone
import docx
from docx.oxml.ns import qn
from docx.oxml import OxmlElement

def paras(d):
    def cell_ps(tables):
        for t in tables:
            for r in t.rows:
                for c in r.cells: yield from c.paragraphs; yield from cell_ps(c.tables)
    yield from d.paragraphs; yield from cell_ps(d.tables)
    for s in d.sections:
        for part in (s.header, s.footer, s.first_page_header, s.first_page_footer):
            yield from part.paragraphs; yield from cell_ps(part.tables)

def find(p, old, start=0):
    full = "".join(r.text for r in p.runs); return full.find(old, start) if old else -1

def rep(p, old, new):
    n = start = 0
    while (i := find(p, old, start)) >= 0:
        pos = 0
        for r in p.runs:  # first run of the match keeps its style and gets the new text
            a, b = pos, pos + len(r.text); pos = b
            if b <= i or a >= i + len(old): continue
            s, e = max(i, a) - a, min(i + len(old), b) - a
            r.text = r.text[:s] + (new if a <= i < b else "") + r.text[e:]
        n += 1; start = i + len(new)
    return n

def isolate(p, i, j):
    """Split runs so text [i, j) sits in whole runs; return those runs."""
    for cut in (i, j):
        pos = 0
        for r in p.runs:
            a, b = pos, pos + len(r.text); pos = b
            if a < cut < b:
                twin = copy.deepcopy(r._r); r._r.addnext(twin)
                t = r.text; r.text = t[:cut - a]; docx.text.run.Run(twin, p).text = t[cut - a:]
                break
    out, pos = [], 0
    for r in p.runs:
        a, b = pos, pos + len(r.text); pos = b
        if a >= i and b <= j and b > a: out.append(r)
    return out

REV = [0]
def mark(tag, author, when):
    el = OxmlElement(tag); REV[0] += 1
    el.set(qn("w:id"), str(90000 + REV[0])); el.set(qn("w:author"), author); el.set(qn("w:date"), when)
    return el

def track(p, old, new, author, when):
    n = start = 0
    while (i := find(p, old, start)) >= 0:
        runs = isolate(p, i, i + len(old)); first = runs[0]._r
        ins_run = copy.deepcopy(first)
        dl = mark("w:del", author, when); first.addprevious(dl)
        for r in runs:
            for t in r._r.findall(qn("w:t")): t.tag = qn("w:delText")
            dl.append(r._r)
        if new:
            ins = mark("w:ins", author, when); dl.addnext(ins); ins.append(ins_run)
            docx.text.run.Run(ins_run, p).text = new
        n += 1; start = i  # deleted text no longer counts in p.runs
    return n

def body_parts(d):
    yield d.element.body
    for s in d.sections:
        for part in (s.header, s.footer, s.first_page_header, s.first_page_footer):
            if part._element is not None: yield part._element

def resolve(d, accept):
    keep, drop = ("w:ins", "w:del") if accept else ("w:del", "w:ins")
    n = 0
    for root in body_parts(d):
        for el in list(root.iter(qn(drop))) + list(root.iter(qn("w:moveFrom" if accept else "w:moveTo"))):
            el.getparent().remove(el); n += 1
        for el in list(root.iter(qn(keep))) + list(root.iter(qn("w:moveTo" if accept else "w:moveFrom"))):
            for t in el.iter(qn("w:delText")): t.tag = qn("w:t")
            parent = el.getparent(); idx = parent.index(el)
            for k, child in enumerate(list(el)): parent.insert(idx + k, child)
            parent.remove(el); n += 1
        for tag in ("w:rPrChange", "w:pPrChange", "w:tblPrChange", "w:trPrChange", "w:tcPrChange", "w:sectPrChange"):
            for el in list(root.iter(qn(tag))):
                if not accept:  # put the old properties back
                    old = el[0] if len(el) else None; holder = el.getparent()
                    if old is not None:
                        for c in list(holder):
                            if c is not el: holder.remove(c)
                        for c in list(old): holder.append(c)
                el.getparent().remove(el); n += 1
    return n

def revisions(d):
    for root in body_parts(d):
        for el in root.iter(qn("w:ins"), qn("w:del")):
            kind = "insert" if el.tag == qn("w:ins") else "delete"
            text = "".join(t.text or "" for t in el.iter(qn("w:t"), qn("w:delText")))
            yield kind, el.get(qn("w:author")), el.get(qn("w:date")), text

ap = argparse.ArgumentParser(); s = ap.add_subparsers(dest="cmd", required=True)
for name in ("show", "revisions"): s.add_parser(name).add_argument("input")
p = s.add_parser("replace"); p.add_argument("input"); p.add_argument("out"); p.add_argument("pairs", nargs="+")
p = s.add_parser("track"); p.add_argument("input"); p.add_argument("out"); p.add_argument("pairs", nargs="+"); p.add_argument("--author", default="Reviewer")
p = s.add_parser("comment"); p.add_argument("input"); p.add_argument("out"); p.add_argument("target"); p.add_argument("text"); p.add_argument("--author", default="Reviewer")
for name in ("accept", "reject"): p = s.add_parser(name); p.add_argument("input"); p.add_argument("out")
p = s.add_parser("fill"); p.add_argument("input"); p.add_argument("out"); p.add_argument("data")
p = s.add_parser("table"); p.add_argument("input"); p.add_argument("out"); p.add_argument("--t", type=int, default=0)
p.add_argument("--add-row", action="append", default=[]); p.add_argument("--set", nargs=3, action="append", default=[])
a = ap.parse_args(); d = docx.Document(a.input)
if a.cmd == "show":
    for i, q in enumerate(d.paragraphs): print(f"{i}\t{q.style.name}\t{q.text[:100]}")
    for i, t in enumerate(d.tables): print(f"table {i}: {len(t.rows)}x{len(t.columns)}; first row: " + " | ".join(c.text for c in t.rows[0].cells))
    revs = list(revisions(d)); print(f"tracked changes: {len(revs)}; comments: {len(list(d.comments))}"); sys.exit()
if a.cmd == "revisions":
    for r in revisions(d): print(*r, sep="\t")
    for c in d.comments: print("comment", c.author, c.text, sep="\t")
    sys.exit()
if os.path.exists(a.out): sys.exit(f"{a.out} exists; pick a new name")
pairs = [x.split("=>", 1) for x in getattr(a, "pairs", [])]
if a.cmd == "replace":
    for o, nw in pairs: print(f"{sum(rep(q, o, nw) for q in paras(d))} x {o!r}")
if a.cmd == "track":
    when = datetime.now(timezone.utc).strftime("%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ")
    for o, nw in pairs: print(f"{sum(track(q, o, nw, a.author, when) for q in paras(d))} x {o!r}")
if a.cmd == "comment":
    for q in paras(d):
        if (i := find(q, a.target)) >= 0:
            runs = isolate(q, i, i + len(a.target)); d.add_comment(runs, text=a.text, author=a.author); print("comment added"); break
    else: sys.exit(f"{a.target!r} not found")
if a.cmd in ("accept", "reject"): print(f"{resolve(d, a.cmd == 'accept')} changes {a.cmd}ed")
if a.cmd == "fill":
    data = json.load(open(a.data))
    for k, v in data.items(): sum(rep(q, "{{" + k + "}}", str(v)) for q in paras(d))
    left = [q.text for q in paras(d) if "{{" in q.text]
    if left: print("still unfilled:", *left, sep="\n  ")
if a.cmd == "table":
    t = d.tables[a.t]
    def put(cell, v):
        ps = cell.paragraphs
        for extra in ps[1:]: extra._p.getparent().remove(extra._p)
        rs = ps[0].runs
        if rs: rs[0].text = v; [r._r.getparent().remove(r._r) for r in rs[1:]]
        else: ps[0].add_run(v)
    for row in a.add_row:
        t._tbl.append(copy.deepcopy(t.rows[-1]._tr))
        for c, v in zip(t.rows[-1].cells, row.split("|")): put(c, v)
    for r, c, v in a.set: put(t.cell(int(r), int(c)), v)
d.save(a.out); print(a.out)
PYEOF
```

## Edit a .docx

`H=~/.file-agent/docx_edit.py`. Every edit writes the new file named second and stops if it exists.

| Job | Command |
|---|---|
| See paragraphs, styles, tables, and counts of tracked changes and comments | `python3 $H show in.docx` |
| Replace text, keep formatting | `python3 $H replace in.docx out.docx "Old Co=>New Co" "2025=>2026"` |
| Replace as tracked changes | `python3 $H track in.docx out.docx "30 days=>15 days" --author "Reviewer"` |
| Add a comment on a phrase | `python3 $H comment in.docx out.docx "1,000 per month" "Is this before tax?"` |
| List tracked changes and comments | `python3 $H revisions in.docx` |
| Accept or reject all tracked changes | `python3 $H accept in.docx out.docx` or `reject` |
| Fill `{{field}}` placeholders from `data.json` | `python3 $H fill template.docx out.docx data.json` |
| Add a row or set a cell in table 0 | `python3 $H table in.docx out.docx --t 0 --add-row "Ink|1|250.00" --set 1 2 "520.00"` |

- Replace, track, and fill work in the body, tables, headers, and footers, and find text split across differently formatted pieces. The new text takes the format of the first piece.
- `fill` lists any placeholder left unfilled. A new table row copies the format of the last row. Rows and columns count from 0, header included.
- For anything else, use python-docx on a copy. Change `run.text`, not `paragraph.text`, because setting `paragraph.text` drops the formatting.
- Text inside links and text boxes is not reached by the helper. If a count is lower than expected, say so.

## Check the result

1. Run `show` on the new file and check the counts.
2. Convert it with `soffice --headless --convert-to pdf --outdir check out.docx`, then `pdftoppm -r 60 -png -f 1 -l 1 check/out.pdf check/p` and look at page 1. Tracked changes show as marked-up text there, which is expected.
3. Reply with the file name or link, what changed, and anything you could not do.
